# What must NEVER reach the image, first — the Dockerfile copies `cloud/` and
# `core/` wholesale, and both directories hold live secrets and data on a
# developer's machine. Without these four lines the built image would ship the
# accounts database, the JWT signing key and the server log to whoever can pull
# it. They are already gitignored; an image is a second way to leak them.
.secrets/
cloud/*.db
cloud/*.db-wal
cloud/*.db-shm
cloud/.jwt_secret
cloud/.backend_id
cloud/*.log
data/

# The rest is build speed. The repo carries ~22MB of model weights and a full
# virtualenv that the API image has no use for; sending them to Fly's remote
# builder on every deploy costs minutes and buys nothing.
.venv/
.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/
.claude-flow/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.onnx
*.pt
benchmarks/
docs/
hardware/
ios/
jupiter/eval/
modules/
services/
site/
tests/
third_party/
typings/
*.csv
